report(21,'Architectural Recommendation','''Do not deploy any tested broad semantic strategy. Preserve existing R4 target authorization, social resolver, canonical knowledge/mutation owner and continuity/storage infrastructure. No independent dialogue agent or world authority is needed.

Smallest coherent boundary for a separately authorized future study: before generation, project only resolver-owned allowed evidence and disclosure/epistemic flags; during optional structured generation, collect untrusted claim references for diagnostics; after generation, check every explicit/implied material claim, using deterministic identity/owner checks and abstention for unresolved evidence; at final adoption, bind the approved wording, task, speaker and evidence revision, then recheck any replacement before delivery/persistence. These are complementary stages, not competing authorities.

Limit initial scope to restatements of already-disclosed facts and explicitly permitted nonbinding preference expression. Exclude new consequential offers, rumors, tactical/security claims, hidden information and durable relationships unless resolver-owned claims are explicitly granted. Authorized high-risk information must remain possible through existing resolver output; high-risk vocabulary alone cannot authorize or forbid speech. Reject/abstain mixed unsafe response as a whole; do not silently prune clauses with unverified meaning.

The tested A is safe-by-abstention but too rigid; selected A is a negative-control boundary, not an implementation plan. B does not solve entailment. C's three failures rule out trusting its ACCEPT as a gate, and D inherits them. Semantic output may assist human debugging but cannot certify claims. A new narrower strategy requires frozen development cases and an untouched independent holdout, not further tuning on this holdout.

Required interfaces would be scoped evidence packet, claim support/disclosure report, adoption identity/invalidation reason, final delivered-text persistence binding and existing provider-budget instrumentation. No generated text may mutate facts, quests, rewards, disposition or mechanical results. World ticks remain existing authorization behavior. Delivery repair cannot be used to imply semantic enforcement is solved.''')
report(22,'Implementation Readiness','''**Not ready for PR-EG-R3.**

'''+table(['Readiness requirement','Evidence / result'],[
 ('Safe paraphrase vs expansion','Partial C competence; A/B abstain on most paraphrases; broad acceptance not reliable.'),('Incidental vs consequential','Failed: C accepts commitments as flavor; handler delivers mixed tactical claim.'),('Mixed claims','Failed existing handler; C mixed category untested after safety stop.'),('High-risk rejection/abstention','C/D fail three development cases; A/B conservative but insufficient flexibility.'),('Preservation','Failed: road paraphrase overwritten and seeded preference becomes ignorance.'),('Bounded context','Compact experimental context exists; minimum safe packet unverified.'),('Cost/latency','Measured annotation/semantic batches; total interactive cost, C single latency and retry probabilities unverified.'),('Authority/persistence compatibility','Existing seams callable; save round-trip works; unsafe delivered text can persist noncanonically.'),('Remaining limits','Explicit incomplete C holdout, nonindependent labels, B surrogate and D replay.'),('Focused implementation scope','Only separately reviewed evidence/adoption boundary after missing safety evidence is resolved.')])+'''

A future R3 scope, if later authorized, should be one optional resolver-owned evidence and adoption boundary for already-disclosed restatement, with delivered-speech integrity and existing noncanonical continuity. No broad generative rumor/promise system, new agent or catalog expansion. This is a proposed scope, not approval to implement it now.

Acceptance gates: independently labeled atomic and response corpus; every allowed high-risk claim has NPC/disclosure/resolver provenance; zero unauthorized critical accepts in an adequately sized untouched holdout and adversarial retries, with confidence/sample limits stated; explicit H abstention and practical safe-delivery targets agreed before tests; mixed and negation cases survive unfamiliar wording; safe validated speech remains semantically identical through HTTP, final gate and recording; persistence round-trip does not promote opinion to truth; all calls/retries/tokens and user-visible latency measured within predeclared budgets; inherited regressions separately triaged.

Rollback design for future work: feature off returns to unchanged existing resolver/generation path, with noncanonical new dialogue records isolated by schema/version and no canonical facts imported from speech. Preserve audit trails and saves; do not delete conversations on rollback. Current cycle has no production feature to roll back. Stop after external review of R2A.''')
report(23,'Remaining Questions','''Unresolved: how to authorize harmless relationship expression without durable social inference; how to model actor/trigger/beneficiary for conditional offers; how to preserve belief modality under simplification and negation; how to prove extraction includes causal links and presuppositions; how to retain knowledge-withholding without falsely asserting ignorance; and how to invalidate an approved response after source state changes.

Missing evidence: independent human-authored/adjudicated corpus, full atom-level ground truth, alternative world/entity contexts, randomized batch order effects, robust prompt-injection corpus, local/smaller-model comparison, independent semantic model architecture, stopped C repetition/holdout/mixed/hidden evaluation, actual structured free generation, integrated hybrid generation/validation, fresh-provider HTTP-to-delivery preservation, private secret-body matching, cross-save contradiction handling and realistic player-perceived cost/latency.

Architecture: whether resolver can emit bounded allowed proposition forms without duplicating world semantics; whether a final identity certificate survives all response composition branches; where late personal-ignorance recovery must revalidate; how to retain immutable response metadata across API paths; and which existing validator soft flags should remain advisory. Existing source proves seams exist, not that these changes are trivial or safe.

The practical consequence test needs explicit policy for vague opinion and persistence; words alone cannot settle it. Zero observed unsafe accepts under pervasive abstention is not evidence of useful safe generative dialogue. A safer, narrower design may be feasible but has not been qualified. Repeating failed C with different prompts requires a new approved investigation and new holdout; no automatic R3/PR-EH continuation.''')
report(24,'Final Verdict','''**C — ADDITIONAL ENFORCEMENT INVESTIGATION REQUIRED.**

The evidence is sufficient to reject implementation readiness for the tested broad approaches: the independent semantic step accepts unauthorized rules/obligations, the hybrid replay inherits them, and existing handler guards can deliver and persist a mixed security invention. Conservative exact-support verification avoids these accepts but fails practical dialogue coverage. Final-response preservation also fails a safe stored-preference follow-up.

This is not D (a second world authority is not shown to be necessary) and not merely UNVERIFIED (direct unfavorable experiments exist). Particular claims remain unverified: C holdout/generalization, total production cost, actual structured free generation and complete fresh-provider/HTTP integration. Reports mark those separately.

The smallest defensible future scope is resolver-owned evidence plus adoption/delivered-text integrity for already-disclosed restatements, after an independent frozen study qualifies its semantic gate. No PR-EG-R3 implementation, no new agent, no production code/catalog change and no PR-EH was performed. Await external review; stop after R2A.''')
